<!doctype html>
<!--
  What the names mean.

  **The garden's ten areas each gather the plants of one theme, and a plant's
  name is what says which.** The head of the genus carries the theme, the ending
  of the genus carries which of the theme's three parts the words under the
  plant are drawn from, and the second word says the one way the plant most
  departs from its genus. None of that was written anywhere a reader could find
  it; it was in docs/NAMES-AND-THEMES.md, `Epithet.swift` and a comment in
  `Areas.swift`. This is the table a reader looks it up in.

  **Drawn, not written out.** Both tables come from `meanings.js`, which the
  block under every area's paragraph is drawn from too, so the short account on
  an area page and the long one here are one table read twice. Each area page
  links to its own row, `/meanings#waiting` and so on.

  Follows the reader's system, light or dark, as the other pages of words do.
  An area page is a night because it is lit by its own sky; this page has none.

  No `noindex`: it publishes no plant anybody grew, only the key to reading
  one, which is the reason `/g` and the areas carry it. Static, like the rest:
  no analytics, no font CDN, no third-party anything.
-->
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Peace Garden — what the names mean</title>
    <meta name="description" content="What brings a plant to each of the garden's ten areas, and what the two words of its name say about it." />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/icon-180.png" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="pool" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <main class="page meanings-page" id="page">
      <!--
        The bar. On every page of the site, and the only way between any two of
        them that is not a link somebody happened to put in a paragraph.
        `site.css` §The bar says why it is the masthead with two things added
        rather than a header of its own.
      -->
      <header class="masthead bar">
        <a class="bar__home" href="/">
          <img class="mark" src="/assets/icon.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
          <span class="wordmark">Peace Garden</span>
        </a>
        <span class="bar__ways">
          <a class="quiet-button" href="/garden" data-s="gardenTitle"></a>
        </span>
      </header>

      <h1 class="heading" data-s="meaningsTitle"></h1>
      <p class="body" data-s="meaningsAbout"></p>

      <!--
        One name, taken apart: each piece of it, and what that piece says. It
        is read back through `passages.js` by `meanings.js`, so it is filed by
        the same rule the passage under a real plant is.
      -->
      <figure class="meanings-example" id="example" hidden></figure>

      <!--
        The ten themes. A table because it is one: ten rows that are read
        across and compared down. On a phone each row becomes a short stack
        with its headings beside the cells, rather than a table the reader has
        to scroll sideways through — see site.css §What the names mean.
      -->
      <div class="meanings-scroll">
        <table class="meanings-table meanings-themes">
          <thead id="themes-head"></thead>
          <tbody id="themes-body"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="body" data-s="meaningsSecond"></p>

      <div class="meanings-scroll">
        <table class="meanings-table meanings-epithets">
          <thead id="epithets-head"></thead>
          <tbody id="epithets-body"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!--
        The foot mirrors the bar: one hairline, above it here where the
        bar's is below, and a row of two things at opposite ends — the
        privacy notice where the mark stands, the language where the way back
        to the garden does.
      -->
      <footer class="foot bar-foot">
        <a class="bar-foot__link" href="/privacy" data-s="privacyTitle"></a>
        <label class="chooser">
          <span class="label" id="language-label"></span>
          <span class="chooser__field">
            <select id="language" class="chooser__select"></select>
            <!-- Monoline, even weight, round free ends, per BRAND.md §3.2. -->
            <svg class="chooser__mark" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path
                d="M4 6.5 L8 10.5 L12 6.5"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.25"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/plain.js"></script>
    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/meaningspage.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
